content.text:
Now the intro overlay is fixed to viewport but the panel is taller than 390, causing internal scroll; the Play button is below the fold, requiring scroll. That's not great in landscape phones. Need a compact intro for short screens:
- In the max-height 620 landscape media, reduce panel padding, h2 font, hide how-to grid or display it as 2 concise rows, reduce lede. Ensure the Start button is visible without scrolling.
- General `.panel { max-height: 100%; overflow-y: auto; }` works but user needs to scroll. Better responsive.

Add CSS @media (max-height: 560px):
.panel { padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 14px; }
.panel .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 4px; font-size: 8px; }
.panel h2 { font-size: 24px; }
.panel .lede { font-size: 10.5px; margin-top: 5px; }
.how { display: none; } or 2 columns compact.
.panel .big-btn { margin-top: 10px; height: 40px; font-size: 12px; min-width: 160px; }
.result-stats margins smaller.
This fits intro in 390: panel ~300. The how-to adds much; hide on short screens (users can use help button). Keep lede and Play.

For pause/gameover/victory short panels fit anyway.

Also the top bar: in screenshot the brand is behind overlay but shown small at top-left, good. HUD maybe full width at 844? hidden by blur.

Let's add the short-screen media query. Also the overlay panel scrollbar shows; hide.

Additionally stage top overlays on very small heights may cover a lot. Fine.

Add:
@media (max-height: 560px) {
 .panel .how { display:none; }
 .panel { padding: 14px 20px; }
 .panel h2 { font-size: 27px; }
 .panel .lede { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 11px; }
 .panel .big-btn { margin-top: 12px; height: 41px; font-size: 12.5px; }
 .panel .ghost-btn { height: 36px; margin-top: 8px; }
 .result-stats { margin: 10px 0 0; }
 .result-stat { padding: 6px 10px; }
 .result-stat b { font-size: 16px; }
}
This will apply to landscape phone 390 height. In portrait 844 height, no.

Also the rotate overlay only for portrait; fine.

Apply.

